# Serena — C0 Session Usage + Review

## Session start (REQUIRED every C0 session)
1. Call `initial_instructions`
2. Call `activate_project` with **`project: "cwn-c0"`** (never `cwn-production` for work in this repo)
3. Call `list_memories` — read `mem:core`, `mem:conventions`, `mem:pipeline` when touching assembly/gates/clip comps

Render/Next.js work in `~/cwn-production` uses **`activate_project("cwn-production")`** instead.

## Code intelligence (C0)

**Reading:** `get_symbols_overview` → `find_symbol` (`include_body=true`) → `find_referencing_symbols`

**Editing `.js`:** `replace_symbol_body` / `replace_content` / `insert_after_symbol` — not StrReplace/Write.

**Non-code** (markdown, yaml, json config, shell): StrReplace/Write OK.

## After EVERY `git commit` on `c0/main`

**Step 1:** `initial_instructions` → `activate_project("cwn-c0")`

**Step 2:** `git diff HEAD~1 --name-only`

**Step 3 — Symbol checks**

| Check | Tool | Pass condition |
|-------|------|----------------|
| Terminology | `find_symbol` "gate N" in strings | No new "gate N" / "Gate N" in comments (schema `gate:` OK) |
| Branding | scan `cwn_production.html` + new platform strings | No new `c0_` prefixes in customer-facing copy; ClipzWorld OK on C0 dashboard |
| Feature gate | `runWorker` / portal extensions | `isFeatureEnabled` before logic |
| Route mounting | new handlers in `server.js` or `lib/routes/*` | Dashboard fetch in `cwn_production.html` or documented API |
| Tests | `test/` | New `lib/*.js` module has `test/*.test.js` |
| Env vars | new `process.env.*` | In `.env.example` or `docs/environment-variables.md` |
| C0 boundary | changed files | No `app/` or Render-only `lib/portals/` commits on `c0/main` |

**Step 4 — Report**
```
✅ Commit QA — [hash] (cwn-c0)
- Files reviewed: N
- Issues: none | [list]
```

Fix issues before the next task.

## Pre-PR (c0/main → auraflux-c0)

Same symbol review on `git diff origin/c0/main...HEAD`. Post `## Serena Review` in PR body.

C0 does **not** auto-deploy Render. No Render curl after push unless cherry-picking to production separately.

## Skipping review

Only if Rob says "skip review" / "just push" — note reason in PR/commit comment.
